{"results":[{"id":"69d50d4138f1353a9d14ce48","name":"APT28 exploit routers to enable DNS hijacking operations","description":"Russian cyber actors APT28 have been exploiting routers to overwrite Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP)\/Domain Name System (DNS) settings to redirect traffic through attacker-controlled DNS servers. Resulting malicious DNS resolutions enable adversary-in-the-middle (AitM) attacks that harvest passwords, OAuth tokens and other credentials for web and email related services. This puts organisations at risk of credential theft, data manipulation and broader compromise.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-05-07T13:00:26.944000","created":"2026-04-07T13:57:21.667000","revision":3,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"APT28","indicators":[{"id":4140866231,"indicator":"CVE-2023-50224","type":"CVE","created":"2026-04-07T13:57:22","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["exploit","tp-link","dns hijacking","russia","oauth","apt28"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1557","T1588","T1584","T1583","T1586","T1190"],"references":["https:\/\/www.ncsc.gov.uk\/news\/apt28-exploit-routers-to-enable-dns-hijacking-operations"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"69d4e63921cbadb426b7cd2a","name":"Detections for the Axios supply chain compromise","description":"A supply chain attack targeting Axios npm package versions 1.14.1 and 0.30.4 introduced a malicious transitive dependency (plain-crypto-js@4.2.1) that executed during installation. The attack deploys cross-platform payloads across Linux, Windows, and macOS through a consistent pattern: Node.js spawns OS-native shells to retrieve and execute remote payloads in detached or hidden contexts. Linux victims receive a Python-based RAT, Windows systems get a PowerShell backdoor with registry persistence, and macOS hosts are compromised with a Mach-O binary backdoor. All variants beacon to the same C2 infrastructure, performing host fingerprinting, process enumeration, filesystem reconnaissance, and arbitrary code execution. The malicious activity is reliably detected through behavioral signatures focusing on unusual Node.js process ancestry and remote payload retrieval rather than static indicators.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-05-07T11:10:38.058000","created":"2026-04-07T11:10:49.715000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":2952018669,"indicator":"process.name","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-07T11:10:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":3550325618,"indicator":"process.parent.name","type":"hostname","created":"2026-04-07T11:10:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4287854984,"indicator":"07d889e2dadce6f3910dcbc253317d28ca61c766","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-04-07T11:10:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4287854988,"indicator":"d6f3f62fd3b9f5432f5782b62d8cfd5247d5ee71","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-04-07T11:10:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4287854999,"indicator":"http:\/\/sfrclak.com:8000\/6202033","type":"URL","created":"2026-04-07T11:10:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4287855002,"indicator":"sfrclak.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-04-07T11:10:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4287959500,"indicator":"92ff08773995ebc8d55ec4b8e1a225d0d1e51efa4ef88b8849d0071230c9645a","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-04-07T11:10:50","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4287970393,"indicator":"58401c195fe0a6204b42f5f90995ece5fab74ce7c69c67a24c61a057325af668","type